WEBVTT

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:10.840
I wonder what exactly makes people shine...

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:32.550
I can almost...

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:36.200
I can almost reach it...

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:43.970
Aaahhhh!

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:45.870
Gasp!

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.030
Whoa!

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:55.740
Ow!

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:58.490
Owww...

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:07.070
Hey! Were you still in bed?!
You'll be late for school!

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:08.420
What?!

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:11.590
Hello, everybody!

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:17.650
The second season starts today!

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:19.720
--Second season?

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:19.720
--Sing and dance like an Uranohoshi
student this season again! Shiny!

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:21.310
--She means the second term.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:21.310
--Sing and dance like an Uranohoshi
student this season again! Shiny!

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:23.430
--At any rate, Chika-<i>chan</i> is late.

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:23.430
--Sing and dance like an Uranohoshi
student this season again! Shiny!

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:28.390
She said she'd get up without
anyone's help, and she's already late...

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.570
I did tell you that you should speak
like a director would, didn't I?

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:36.530
You were supposed to say,
"Please behave in a way befitting

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:38.910
an Uranohoshi student and study hard."

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:40.490
"Behave in a way befouling"?

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:41.870
"Befitting"!

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:44.830
In any case, it was close.

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:48.040
Yeah. I heard we almost
made it to the nationals.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:51.040
There's no point in dwelling 
on the past, <i>zura</i>.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:53.170
But...!

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:56.510
Why is the prize for participating
a two-color ballpoint pen?

00:01:56.510 --> 00:01:59.760
Maybe you get a three-color one
if you make it to the nationals?

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:01.550
It's the future, <i>zura</i>!

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:02.470
How is it the future?!

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:05.390
Shut up!

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:11.980
It was indeed disappointing
that we couldn't make it to the nationals.

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:16.490
But we were able to turn a zero into a one.

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:19.200
It was all thanks to you, everyone.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:22.240
And...

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:22.990
Now...

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:25.910
The number of prospective students
went from one to ten as well!

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:27.410
True.

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:29.590
That's not all.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:34.460
They announced the next Love Live today.

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:35.550
Love Live?!

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.420
"Chika Takami"

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:37.380
Really?!

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:38.420
Yes.

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:43.180
Just like the previous ones,
the final competition will be at Akiba Dome!

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:46.640
--Too late!
--You're very late!

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:50.140
Next Love Live...

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:52.190
--Chika-<i>chan</i>!
--What do you wanna do?

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.570
I don't think we need to ask.

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:56.940
Yoshiko-<i>chan</i> has been waiting, too, <i>zura</i>!

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.570
--Yep!
--It's Yohane!

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:03.190
Let's enter Love Live!

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:09.870
And... And we'll turn one into ten,
and ten into a hundred!

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:11.220
And we'll save the school!

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:14.350
--And then...
--And then?!

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:18.960
And then, I think we'll be able
to shine in our own way!

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:20.370
I'm sure...

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:24.070
We can shine!

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:40.240
<i>Let's throw our all at each other</i>
<i>and grab hold of the future!</i>

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:50.870
<i>The sky and this ocean are both on our side</i>

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:54.830
<i>Shining and saying, "Go, do your best!"</i>

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:01.550
<i>To let our voices reach far, far away</i>

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:06.470
<i>Shall we shout our dreams louder?</i>

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:08.220
<i>(Full of hope)</i>

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:12.560
<i>Today pulls tomorrow toward itself</i>

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:21.150
<i>It's really fun to grasp the magnet</i>
<i>in my heart and run right now!</i>

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:23.280
<i>(Let's always go together)</i>

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:26.160
<i>What shall we do about the future?!</i>

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:33.870
<i>Everyone laughs and cries as</i>
<i>they look for the shape of their dreams</i>

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:42.300
<i>Because I'm sure the</i>
<i>future us will have the answer</i>

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:50.390
<i>Let's run with everything we have</i>
<i>and become the shining wind</i>

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:53.390
<i>We got dream</i>

00:04:55.600 --> 00:05:00.020
One, two, three, four... Okay.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:01.030
"#1 Next Step"

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:02.940
Your body is as stiff as ever, Yoshiko-<i>chan</i>.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:04.980
Are you stretching every day?

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:06.530
It's Yohane!

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:09.530
That's not good enough.

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:11.080
--Ow, ow, ow, ow!
--Here, I'll push you.

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:12.450
Hold on a sec!

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:14.620
This body is merely a temporary vessel!

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:16.670
The fallen angel's true form is...

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:18.950
Ow, ow, owwww!

00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:21.380
You've become quite flexible, Hanamaru-<i>chan</i>.

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:24.340
I'm stretching at home every day, <i>zura</i>.

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:25.880
I'm doing push-ups, too.

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:26.750
Really?!

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:28.480
Just watch, <i>zura</i>.

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:37.190
Onnnnnnnnnnne!

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:38.480
Gulp.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:39.730
That was perfect, <i>zura</i>.

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:41.820
That was amazing, Hanamaru-<i>chan</i>!

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:43.030
It's miracle!

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:44.070
A miracle how?!

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:47.570
So when is the next Love Live going to be?

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:50.660
It's probably next spring.

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:53.290
Bzzzzt!

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:56.330
There's something we need to do before that!

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:58.460
--What?
--Have you forgotten?

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:00.710
We need to increase the number
of prospective students, right?

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:03.960
School... open house...

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:05.210
Oh, that's right.

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:08.340
"Come join us!!"
"Uranohoshi Girls' High School"
"Open House"

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:08.340
Of course! I've already
made an announcement.

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:12.850
This is a good opportunity.
Let's hold a concert for the participants

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:15.810
and show how appealing our school is!

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:16.730
That's a good idea!

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:19.420
I think that's a very good idea!

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:24.360
You were in the bathroom forever!
We've already started practice!

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:26.530
Can you afford to worry about others?

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:28.570
Ow, ow, owwww!

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:32.200
"Incoming call"
"Slide to answer"

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:41.540
Oh, that's right. The bus service
stops running earlier in the fall.

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:47.340
"Uranohoshi Girls' High School"
"Tokai Bus Stop"

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:43.130
That's right, <i>zura</i>.

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:47.340
The sun sets sooner too, so our practice time
after school may become shorter.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:50.840
There aren't many days left
before the school open house.

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:53.050
I know, but...

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:56.170
We need to be serious about ensuring
we have enough time to practice.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:07:00.060
Shall we start
two hours earlier in the morning?

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:04.570
--Okay, then, it's decided!
--That's too early!

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:09.990
You were also told to come home
a little earlier, right, Yoshiko-<i>chan</i>?

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:13.320
Gack! H-How'd you know that?

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:19.450
Well, it seems like my mom spoke
with your mom a lot at Love Live.

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:22.880
Well then, in the name of the fallen angel...

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:23.660
Yoshiko?

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:27.550
Hey! Open the door.

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:28.810
The name is Yohane!

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:32.550
--Hey, Yoshiko! Open the door.

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:32.550
--I heard that you wouldn't
let her come in to your room.

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:35.850
Th-That's because Yohane is a fallen angel,

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:39.020
so Mother is basically a temporary housemate.

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:41.060
What's her mom like?

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:43.100
I heard that she's a school teacher.

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:46.320
Since Yoshiko-<i>chan</i> didn't let her
nursing bottle go until kindergarten,

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:47.820
--her mom had to...
--Ahhh!

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:52.950
Wait... I wonder if the buses that
head this way from Numazu run late...

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:58.580
"Uranohoshi Girls' High School"
"Tokai Bus Stop"

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:57.090
There are people who're
coming back from work, so...

00:07:57.950 --> 00:08:01.790
Ah... We can practice in Numazu!

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:04.380
We can ensure we have enough
practice time that way, <i>zura</i>!

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:05.540
I'm all for it!

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:08.000
Yeah. What do you think, Mari?

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:10.850
Hm? No problem!

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:13.630
Okay, then, it's decided!

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:17.300
Let's find a place
to practice together tomorrow.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:20.180
I'll recruit more little demons!

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:22.350
Yoshiko-<i>chan</i>, you're overly zealous, <i>zura</i>.

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:23.350
It's Yohane!

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:28.760
See you tomorrow!

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:34.410
It's beautiful.

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:37.740
It is.

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:44.790
You know... For a second...
It was really only for a second,

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:47.750
but I think singing together
with everyone at the prelims

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:51.090
helped me understand
what it means to shine.

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:53.010
Is that right?

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:54.760
Yep, of course!

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:11.810
It may just be a little,
but I'm sure we can shine.

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:15.960
If we try hard, we can definitely shine!
That's how I felt.

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:19.660
Yeah, it seems tough, but...

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:21.700
That's what makes it worth it.

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:34.170
But you promised me that you'd wait, Dad!
This is too sudden!

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:46.690
Thank you for waiting!

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:48.440
What happened?

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:51.860
Sorry! I can't speak Japanese.

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:53.650
Something happened, right?!

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:58.800
What're you talking about?

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:00.600
I'll sue you.

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:03.370
Wait, wait...

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:06.620
I guess I have no choice. The truth is...

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:07.870
The truth is...?

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:11.540
I gained a little weight lately,
so I've been feeling blue.

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:15.420
That's a lie. It hasn't changed.

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:17.420
How do you know?

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:22.030
I can tell. Besides, you wouldn't feel blue
over something petty like that.

00:10:22.030 --> 00:10:22.720
So what is it?

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:25.080
Mari!

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:29.680
What... do we do?

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:33.530
Mari...

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:43.990
Chika-<i>chan</i>, were you able
to find a good place?

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:47.450
Well... it's pretty hard to find one.

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:49.290
Your family runs a temple, right, Zuramaru?

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:50.870
Isn't there a great hall or something?

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:54.880
Are you really sure you wanna
use our temple, <i>zura</i>?

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:58.590
Also, our place is pretty far,
so it won't work, <i>zura</i>.

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:01.140
Then Yoshiko-<i>chan</i>'s house might be better.

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:04.470
And just where do you think
we'd have space to practice?!

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:10.690
Hm? Where did Dia-<i>san</i> and the others go?

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:13.020
They were here up until just earlier.

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:15.690
It looked like Mari-<i>san</i> had a phone call.

00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:19.780
So it can no longer be overturned?

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:21.990
No, it can't be over.

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:27.000
--Kanan...
--Does Dia know about this?

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:29.380
How could I tell her?

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:33.290
Then you should do a better job of hiding it.

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:35.040
Dia!

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:41.540
You've been acting suspicious
for a while. That's definitely bzzzzt!

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:44.300
Wow...

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:46.180
This is spacious!

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:48.140
This is amazing!

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:52.140
When you open this, there's a mirror, too!

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:54.510
Now, let us journey into the mirror world!

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:56.860
Give it a rest, <i>zura</i>.

00:11:57.400 --> 00:11:59.900
My dad's acquaintance is renting this space,

00:11:59.900 --> 00:12:01.860
but he said he won't be using it for a while.

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:04.660
--Just as you'd expect from a ship captain!
--It's not like he sailed us here.

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:07.870
Moreover, there are many stores
on our way home!

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:11.080
You shouldn't think about
having fun all the time like that.

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:13.790
--There's a bookstore, too, <i>zura</i>!
--Really?!

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:14.880
Riko-<i>chan</i>...

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:18.590
Well then, why don't we
check our formation?

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:20.120
Yeah!

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:21.590
Hold on a sec.

00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:25.050
Before that, there's something
we need to tell you.

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:26.420
Something to tell us?

00:12:27.050 --> 00:12:29.060
Yeah. To tell you the truth...

00:12:29.930 --> 00:12:30.630
Mari...

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:34.140
To tell you the truth,
the school open house...

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:37.060
...will be canceled.

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:46.090
<i>Love Live! Sunshine!!</i>

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:47.120
"Love Live! Sunshine!!"

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:50.370
Canceled?

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:52.370
What do you mean?

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:54.620
It means exactly what it sounds like.

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:56.160
The school open house will be canceled.

00:12:56.670 --> 00:13:00.340
Uranohoshi High will officially
stop recruiting students for the next year.

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:01.260
Oh no...

00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:02.800
Isn't it too sudden?

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:06.360
She's right, <i>zura</i>!
The second term only just started.

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:07.010
Yeah.

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:10.100
From the students' perspective,
it may seem that way.

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:12.430
But the school has been
considering combining it

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:14.390
with another school for the past two years.

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:18.860
Mari tried hard to persuade her dad,
so it was postponed until now.

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:22.150
But there've been more
prospective students, right?

00:13:22.150 --> 00:13:24.360
We had zero first, but now we have ten.

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:27.420
I'm sure we'll have more and more.

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:29.970
Of course I told him that.

00:13:29.970 --> 00:13:33.830
But that alone wasn't enough 
to overturn the decision.

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:35.870
Mari-<i>chan</i>! Where's he?

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:37.620
Chika-<i>chi</i>?

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:39.920
--I'll go talk to him!
--Chika-<i>chan</i>!

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:44.470
Wait! He's in America!
Mari-<i>san</i>'s dad is in America!

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:45.910
Isn't that right?

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:48.390
Yes.

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:51.220
I'll ask Mito-<i>nee</i>, Shima-<i>nee</i>, and my mom.

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:56.230
I'll ask for my allowance in advance
and borrow even more, and go to America.

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:57.390
And...

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:01.150
I'll ask him to wait a little bit longer.

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:02.980
Chika-<i>chan</i>...

00:14:02.980 --> 00:14:04.360
Do you really think that will work?

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:05.460
It will!

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:11.040
Now that it's come to this,
I'll use my special ability!

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:17.960
Mari loves our school... She loves our town.

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:22.540
She's been putting the school before
studying abroad and her own future.

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:27.260
She's been trying so hard
to keep our school alive.

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:32.180
She's been working hard
as the director behind the scenes.

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:36.890
If Mari herself is telling us that
we can't do anything about it this time...

00:14:37.270 --> 00:14:38.920
But... But...!

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:45.560
Chika-<i>chi</i>... I'm sorry. Tee-hee.

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:53.290
No... I didn't mean it that way. I didn't...

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:03.710
If we had won at the
regional prelims that time...

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:06.310
...and were able to go to the nationals,

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:08.220
I wonder...

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:11.220
if we could've
changed the future...

00:15:16.770 --> 00:15:17.980
I wonder if the future...

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:24.400
...would've been different...

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:30.530
You'll be...

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:33.440
...getting your winter fur soon, huh?

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:36.490
"Tochiman Inn"

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:36.490
You're home late today.

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:38.330
Yeah.

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:42.180
Oh yeah. Mu-<i>chan</i> and
the others came by earlier.

00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:46.840
"Go for Love Live!"

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:55.050
This...

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:57.680
Yeah. Your friends made it together,
so she brought it for you.

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:00.260
She said everyone's rooting for you guys.

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:03.850
Chika-<i>chan</i>? What's wrong?

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:07.060
Nothing. Thanks!

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:14.030
For various reasons, our school
open house has been canceled.

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:17.740
And it's been officially decided
that Uranohoshi Girls' High School

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:19.790
will be combined with another school
and closed down next year.

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:21.120
Oh no...

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:25.880
To those of you who've been preparing
for the open house... I'm very sorry,

00:16:21.800 --> 00:16:23.090
--Is that final?

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:30.760
but since it's been canceled, please take
down posters and such immediately.

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:34.220
I wonder if there's really nothing we can do.

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:38.100
A problem like this is out of our league.

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:42.600
If something could be done, Chika and
the others would've done it already.

00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:53.620
What a beautiful sunset...

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:58.950
How things turned out is,
of course, unfortunate.

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:01.870
But I'm glad that we worked so hard.

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:09.980
Unlike Tokyo, this is a small seaside town.
And yet, we were able to come this far.

00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:12.920
Do you really mean that?

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:18.100
If you really mean that,

00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:22.780
I despise you.

00:17:26.150 --> 00:17:27.610
Roar!

00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:31.110
Beep, boom!

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:33.990
I'm the normal monster, Riko-<i>pi</i>!

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:36.280
Take this! Riko-<i>chan</i> Beam!

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:38.120
Did I do it right?

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:41.390
You're finally smiling.

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:46.920
I'm an Aqours member, too, you know.

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:50.500
I thought I'd continue
to sing together with you guys.

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:52.880
I thought I'd make lots of songs, too.

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:56.590
I'd never think that this is okay. Never...

00:17:57.220 --> 00:17:58.230
Riko-<i>chan</i>...

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:01.260
I don't know what we should do...

00:18:02.240 --> 00:18:03.720
I just don't know...

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:15.930
Chika! Aren't you eating dinner?!

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:32.500
The school open house... will be canceled.

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:39.840
I just don't know...

00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:43.510
"Go for Love Live!"

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:10.580
"Tochiman Inn"

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:08.370
Morning! See you later!

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:09.080
Chika?!

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:10.580
Huh?

00:19:32.060 --> 00:19:36.650
Roooooooar!

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:43.170
I'll make...
a miracle happen no matter what!

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:47.950
Until then...

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:49.910
...I won't cry...

00:19:50.530 --> 00:19:51.920
I'm not gonna cry!

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:54.790
I knew you'd come.

00:19:57.550 --> 00:19:59.360
You-<i>chan</i>... How'd you...?

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:03.050
I don't know, but... look.

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:07.640
Everyone...

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:09.980
When I noticed, I was here.

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:12.070
Mari-<i>chan</i>...

00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:14.430
We're on the same wavelength, <i>zura</i>.

00:20:14.430 --> 00:20:15.150
Yep!

00:20:16.230 --> 00:20:18.900
A whisper from the darkness called me here.

00:20:18.900 --> 00:20:21.320
I don't really get what happened, though...

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:24.990
You don't? I do. I bet...

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:27.740
I bet we don't want to give up.

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:30.870
We just don't want to give up!

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:33.250
I know Mari-<i>chan</i>
tried very hard all this time.

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:37.670
But I haven't... the rest of us
haven't done anything yet.

00:20:37.670 --> 00:20:38.500
You're right.

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:40.540
We may be wasting our time...

00:20:40.540 --> 00:20:43.230
but I want us to try until the very end.

00:20:43.230 --> 00:20:44.390
I want us to struggle!

00:20:45.090 --> 00:20:47.600
I want to search for
the shine that I glimpsed.

00:20:48.930 --> 00:20:49.840
I want to find it.

00:20:50.390 --> 00:20:53.520
You never did know when to give up, Chika.

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:55.810
Neither do you, Kanan-<i>san</i>.

00:20:55.810 --> 00:20:57.230
--And you, either, Sis.
--What?

00:21:02.280 --> 00:21:03.490
So what do you think?

00:21:10.290 --> 00:21:12.840
Chika-<i>chi</i>... Everyone...

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:17.440
Why not? Why don't we
struggle as hard as we can?

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:21.700
Yeah. If we're going to do it,
let's shoot for a miracle!

00:21:22.210 --> 00:21:23.170
A miracle!

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:24.430
A miracle!

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:25.680
A miracle!

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:26.930
A miracle!

00:21:27.220 --> 00:21:28.140
A miracle!

00:21:28.430 --> 00:21:29.300
A miracle!

00:21:29.640 --> 00:21:30.510
A miracle!

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:51.310
Wow...

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:00.170
--Chika-<i>chan</i>!
--Chika-<i>chan</i>!

00:22:02.050 --> 00:22:03.590
Let's make a miracle happen!

00:22:04.170 --> 00:22:06.090
Let's struggle as hard as we can!

00:22:06.840 --> 00:22:13.460
Let's give it all we've got!
Let's shine together until the very end!

00:22:15.350 --> 00:22:18.310
<i>Try and be brave</i>

00:22:18.310 --> 00:22:20.770
<i>I know it's actually scary</i>

00:22:20.770 --> 00:22:26.780
<i>It's not like I was able to</i>
<i>do it from the start, either</i>

00:22:26.780 --> 00:22:29.620
<i>I messed up a lot</i>

00:22:29.620 --> 00:22:32.280
<i>I was really frustrated</i>

00:22:32.280 --> 00:22:37.830
<i>But</i> <i>that</i> <i>gave</i> <i>me</i> <i>strength,</i>
<i>so</i> <i>just</i> <i>don't</i> <i>give</i> <i>up</i>

00:22:37.830 --> 00:22:43.550
<i>Tears</i> <i>in</i> <i>your</i> <i>eyes</i>
<i>that</i> <i>want</i> <i>to</i> <i>try</i> <i>believing</i>

00:22:43.550 --> 00:22:47.800
<i>Say "bye-bye" to hesitation and tears</i>

00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:49.470
<i>Now, let's go!</i>

00:22:49.470 --> 00:22:54.640
<i>Let's chase them as</i>
<i>many times as it takes, don't lose</i>

00:22:54.640 --> 00:22:57.890
<i>Everyone fails sometimes</i>

00:22:57.890 --> 00:23:00.940
<i>But dreams won't fade, dreams won't fade</i>

00:23:00.940 --> 00:23:06.320
<i>Let's chase them as</i>
<i>many times as it takes, don't lose</i>

00:23:06.320 --> 00:23:14.370
<i>'Cause today is today, and once</i>
<i>you wake up, it'll be a new morning</i>

00:23:14.370 --> 00:23:22.380
<i>Oh, the sun's smiling down on you</i>

00:23:36.350 --> 00:23:38.770
Next Time! "The Sound of Rain."

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:41.600
"#2 The Sound of Rain"
